  "answer_text": "Found 2 gene records and 5 disease records for MLH1, MSH2 and colorectal cancer [2][3][4][5][6][7][8]. \n\nMLH1 was identified as a locus frequently mutated in hereditary nonpolyposis colon cancer (HNPCC) [1]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene NCBIGene:4292, name: mutL homolog 1 [2]. Gene NCBIGene:4436, name: mutS homolog 2 [6]. Gene symbol: MLH1 [9]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Muir-Torr\u00c3\u00a9 syndrome [3]. Disease name: Colorectal cancer, hereditary nonpolyposis, type 2 [4]. Disease name: Mismatch repair cancer syndrome 1 [5]. Disease name: Lynch syndrome 1 [7]. Disease name: Mismatch repair cancer syndrome 2 [8]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Functional analysis of human MLH1 variants using yeast and in vitro mismatch repair assays [10]. Pubmed title: Novel 2-Benzoyl-6-(2,3-Dimethoxybenzylidene)-Cyclohexenol Confers Selectivity toward Human MLH1 Defective Cancer Cells through Synthetic Lethality [14]. Pubmed title: Methylation Tolerance-Based Functional Assay to Assess Variants of Unknown Significance in the MLH1 and MSH2 Genes and Identify Patients With Lynch Syndrome [17]. Pubmed title: Clinicopathological and molecular characterization of deficient mismatch repair colorectal cancer [20]. Pubmed title: AI-generated MLH1 small binder improves prime editing efficiency [23]. \n\nClinvar records found\n\nClinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.545+1271_677+737delinsCA [11]. Clinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.453+625_545+920delinsT [15]. Clinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.1418A>T (p.His473Leu) [18]. Clinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.884+5T>A [21]. Clinvar title: NM_000249.4(MLH1):c.1039-1013G>A [24]. \n\nOmim records found\n\nDNA MISMATCH REPAIR PROTEIN MLH1 [12]. MLH1 [12]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: The IMPACT Study - Identification of Men With a Genetic Predisposition to ProstAte Cancer [13]. Clinical trial name: Study of MK-3475 in Patients With Microsatellite Unstable (MSI) Tumors (Cohort